---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const backend = `import { createCopyPatchBackend } from '@copypatch/backend';
import { createSQLitePersistence } from '@copypatch/storage-sqlite';

const persistence = createSQLitePersistence('./data/copypatch.sqlite');
await persistence.migrate();

export const copypatch = createCopyPatchBackend({
  persistence,
  passphraseHash: process.env.COPYPATCH_PASSPHRASE_HASH!,
});`;
---

<DocsLayout title="Backend and adapters" description="Create an embedded CopyPatch v2 backend and mount it through the host framework adapter.">
  <h1>Backend and adapters</h1>
  <p class="lead">The v2 backend is a library instance owned by your application, not an independent CopyPatch server process.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={backend} lang="ts" title="lib/copypatch.ts" />

  <h2>Persistence</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>@copypatch/storage-sqlite</code> uses a local SQLite file and fits a single server or development environment.</li>
    <li><code>@copypatch/storage-postgres</code> shares state between application instances through PostgreSQL.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>
  <p>Pass a <code>passphraseHash</code> for CopyPatch-managed sessions, or pass an <code>authAdapter</code> that returns host principals with <code>editor</code> and <code>publisher</code> roles and verifies each mutation.</p>

  <h2>Node adapters</h2>
  <p><code>@copypatch/node</code> exports native Node, Express, Fastify, and Hono adapters. Each mounts the same backend at <code>/__copypatch/api/v2</code> in the host application.</p>

  <p><code>@copypatch/server</code> is the v1 standalone package. It is deprecated for new integrations, will retire in a later major release, and will not be unpublished.</p>
</DocsLayout>
